Official hazard is an SGC product for periods of hundreds of years. It must not be confused with this platform's experimental forecast.
The sidebar, the glass top bar and the phone's bottom navigation are the ones on this very page.
The search for similar periods is only available in the trained configurations.
It is officially computed by the Colombian Geological Survey with seismogenic source and attenuation models. It is expressed, for example, as peak ground acceleration (PGA) for a return period of {0} years. It is not the same as this platform's experimental {1}-day forecast.
Quality A–D is a code derived in this project (gap, horizontal error and RMS); it is not an official SGC code.
Complexity is only accepted if it improves on the baseline.
The visual link between two events only indicates that they occurred close in space and time. It does not imply physical causality or that one triggered the other.
