The optional relief, reference map and official hazard layers request images from third-party servers (AWS, OpenStreetMap and SGC), which receive your IP address as in any web visit. They are off by default.
The estimates are experimental and separate from official products. Colombia's official seismic hazard is computed by the Colombian Geological Survey for return periods of hundreds of years; here it is shown only as a reference layer.
The ripples are a visual representation of the event, not an exact physical simulation.
Depths < {0} or > {1} km become missing. A depth of exactly {2} km usually indicates a depth fixed by the analyst; it is flagged, not discarded.
Aftershocks cluster activity in time and space. If a single sequence is split between training and test, the metrics are inflated.
The breaks detected mainly reflect the evolution of the network and the processing. That is why the models are evaluated on recent blocks and long series are interpreted with caution.
Aftershock sequences raise the metrics of models that use recent activity; the leakage detector warns about it.
Variables use only the past.
