Brier gain
Brier gain = {0} − model Brier / baseline Brier. ECE = expected calibration error. σ PR-AUC = standard deviation between time blocks.
Brier gain over the baseline
Relative improvement in the Brier score with respect to historical frequency. To the right, better than the baseline; to the left, worse. A value close to zero means the added complexity contributes nothing.
