There was no event
Not reported (imported file)
We do not try to anticipate an isolated earthquake. We divide the territory into zones and time into periods. Each zone, at each date, is described only by its past, and we note whether there was at least one event above the threshold in the following thirty days.
Do not mix official seismic hazard with this platform's experimental probability.
Do not present hypothetical scenarios as facts or hide the uncertainty when sharing results.
I cannot answer that: nobody can predict when or where an earthquake will occur, and this platform does not issue alerts. What I can show you is the recorded activity and the estimated probability by zone, with its uncertainty. For official information and preparedness advice, consult the Colombian Geological Survey and the National Unit for Disaster Risk Management.
Not reported
No official download service with a documented licence was confirmed; the layer is not included.
It is not chosen by accuracy.
When, exactly where or how large an earthquake will be is not estimated. Nor is damage estimated: that is risk, and it requires exposure and vulnerability data that this project does not include.
They were not homogenised to Mw; an “M ≥ {0}” threshold combines ML, MLr and others.
Exposure and vulnerability are not included: the results do not measure risk or expected damage.
No replacement values are shown: the view stays empty until the real data are available.
Individual earthquakes are not predicted: the estimates are probabilities by zone and period.
Individual earthquakes are not predicted. Large events are very scarce, the catalogue changed system in twenty eighteen, and we do not include exposure or vulnerability. This platform does not replace the Colombian Geological Survey or risk management authorities.
Did not flag
I have no information to answer that with the platform's data, and I would rather not make things up. I can help with event filters, comparisons between departments, recent activity, definitions and models. Try one of the examples.
Do not use the results as an alert, an official notice or a basis for decisions on evacuation, civil protection, insurance or investment.
No. It does not issue alerts or predict individual earthquakes. For official information consult the Colombian Geological Survey and risk management authorities.
